","The correct answer is $\boxed{\text{(a) Al}_2\text{O}_3}$.  

**Explanation:**  
- The reduction of metal oxides by carbon involves the displacement of oxygen by carbon, forming carbon monoxide (CO) or carbon dioxide (CO₂).  
- The reactivity of metal oxides decreases as the ionization energy of the metal increases.  
- Aluminum has a very high ionization energy, making Al₂O₃ highly stable and resistant to reduction by carbon.  
- The other metal oxides (PbO, ZnO, Fe₂O₃) have lower ionization energies and can be reduced by carbon.  

Thus, Al₂O₃ is the metal oxide that cannot be reduced to metal by carbon.
