Given the function $f(x)=\sin (\omega x+\varphi )$ $(\omega > 0,0 < \varphi < \frac{\pi}{2})$, $f(0)=-f( \frac{\pi}{2} )$, if the graph of $f(x)$ is translated to the right by $\frac{\pi}{12}$ units and the resulting function's graph is symmetric about the origin, then $\varphi=$ ( )

