\]

Since \(\mathbf{V}(x, y)\) depends only on \(x\) and \(y\), its components are:

\[
\mathbf{V} = \mathbf{i} \phi(x, y) + \mathbf{j} \psi(x, y) + \mathbf{k} 0
\]

Substituting this into the curl expression:

\[
\nabla \times \mathbf{V} = \left( \frac{\partial 0}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial \psi}{\partial z} \right)\mathbf{i} + \left( \frac{\partial 0}{\partial z} - \frac{\partial \phi}{\partial x} \right)\mathbf{j} + \left( \frac{\partial \psi}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial \phi}{\partial y} \right)\mathbf{k}
\]

