- \( \frac{d^2x}{dt^2} \) is the second derivative of displacement \( x \) with respect to time \( t \), which represents acceleration.
- \( b \) is the damping coefficient, which represents the resistance to motion due to damping.
- \( \frac{dx}{dt} \) is the first derivative of displacement \( x \) with respect to time \( t \), which represents velocity.
- \( k \) is the spring constant, which represents the stiffness of the spring.

