What is the net chemical reaction that occurs during the discharging of a lead storage battery?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The net chemical reaction during the discharging of a lead storage battery is:
\[ \text{Pb(s)} + \text{PbO}_2(\text{s}) + 2\text{H}^+(aq) + 2\text{e}^- \rightarrow 2\text{Pb(OH)}_2(\text{s}) \]
This reaction can be broken down into two half-reactions:
1. **Oxidation at the anode (Pb electrode):**
   \[ \text{Pb(s)} + \text{H}_2\text{O(l)} \rightarrow \text{Pb(OH)}_2(\text{s}) + 2\text{e}^- \]
2. **Reduction at the cathode (PbO₂ electrode):**
   \[ \text{PbO}_2(\text{s}) + 2\text{H}^+(aq) + 2\text{e}^- \rightarrow \text{Pb(OH)}_2(\text{s}) \]
