\]
The threshold voltage is shifted by \(-1.0\) V, so the new threshold voltage is:
\[
V_T = 0.31 \text{ V} - 1.0 \text{ V} = -0.69 \text{ V}
\]
Using the equation for the threshold voltage, we can solve for \(V_{BS}\):
\[
-0.69 \text{ V} = 0.31 \text{ V} + \alpha V_{BS}
