     \[
     \text{Mass of TNT} = \frac{E_{\text{total}}}{\text{Energy per gram of TNT}} = \frac{3.42 \times 10^6}{4680} = 725 \text{ g}
     \]

**Final Answer:**
The mass of TNT required to release the same energy is \(\boxed{725 \text{ g}}\).
