   The pressure ratio is:
   \[
   \frac{P_2}{P_1} = r^2 = 2.55^2 = 6.4525
   \]
   The temperature ratio is:
   \[
   \frac{T_2}{T_1} = r^{k-1} = 2.55^{0.4} = 1.55
   \]
   Substituting the initial pressure (\( P_1 = 0.1 \text{ MPa} \)) and temperature (\( T_1 = 60 + 273 = 333 \text{ K} \)):
   \[
   P_2 = 6.4525 \times 0.1 \text{ MPa} = 0.645 \text{ MPa}
